 result←object style arg;bits;props;style;was

⍝ 0 = Vertical (right/left)
⍝ 1 = Horizontal (bottom/top)
⍝ 2 = Size box (corner)
⍝    Select one (ignored except during creation, so they've already been handled):
⍝ +0 = No alignment (floating)
⍝ +4 = Bottom/right alignment
⍝ +8 = Top/left alignment

 style←object ⎕VGET⊂'_style' 0 ⍝ What style were we?
 :If 0=≢arg
     result←style
 :Else
     '∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: style'##.##.Error~##.##.IsInt arg←##.##.Single arg
     '∆WI ATTRIBUTE ERROR: Invalid "style" attribute specified'##.##.Error∨/∊arg<0
     arg←+/bits←##._supp.SetBitVals arg
     '∆WI ATTRIBUTE ERROR: Invalid "style" attribute specified'##.##.Error×≢bits~0 1 2 4 8
     '∆WI ATTRIBUTE ERROR: Invalid "style" attribute specified'##.##.Error(∧/1 2∊bits)∨∧/4 8∊bits
     object._style←arg
     was←##.##.BitVals style ⍝ Previous bit settings

     :If (1∊was)≠1∊bits ⍝ If the orientation flag has not changed, then we don't need to mess with it
         props←0⍴⊂''
         props,←0/⊂'VScroll'(-1∊bits) ⍝ Changing orientation will not change size/where     ⍝? Create-only
         props,←0/⊂'HScroll'(-2∊bits) ⍝ Changing orientation will not change size/where     ⍝? Create-only
         ⍝object ##.##.∆WS props ⍝? Nothing changeable here ATM
     :EndIf

     :If (2∊was)≠2∊bits ⍝ If the corner flag has not changed, then we don't need to mess with it
         ⍝? How in the world are we going to manage this non-destructively???
         :If 2∊bits ⍝ Switch from a scroll bar to a corner
             ##.##.Error'Scroll bar cannot currently be changed to a corner shape'
         :Else ⍝ Switch from a corner to a scroll bar
             ##.##.Error'Corner shape cannot currently be changed to a scroll bar'
         :EndIf
     :EndIf

     :If (4 8∊was)≢4 8∊bits ⍝ If the alignment flags have not changed, then we don't need to mess with it
        ⍝ But changing alignment has no effect on an existing control anyway
     :EndIf

     result←##.NoRes
 :EndIf
